s in.","type":"text"}],"title":"Forest","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/forest"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/OrderedTree":{"abstract":[{"text":"An ordered tree (plane tree): a rooted tree in which the children of each vertex form a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sequence, first to last. The order is part of the value: two ordered trees are equal when they","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"have the same root and every vertex has the same children in the same order, which is the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identity being an ordered-tree isomorphism between them.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/orderedtree","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OrderedTree","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OrderedTree","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/OrderedTree","kind":"symbol","title":"OrderedTree"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Arborescence":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Arborescence","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Arborescence","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Arborescence","type":"topic","title":"Arborescence","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/arborescence","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An arborescence: a directed tree whose edges all point away from its root, so every vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but the root has exactly one incoming edge, from its parent. As a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" are the children, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"predecessors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the parent (zero or one), and each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedEdge(from: parent, to: child)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/Tree":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A tree: a connected, acyclic undirected graph with at least one vertex, so it has exactly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"n − 1 edges, no self-loop and no parallel edges. The invariant is the type: every initializer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from unchecked input is failable, and a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Tree"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot be mutated."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/tree","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Tree","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Tree","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Tree","kind":"symbol","title":"Tree"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/Trees-Arborescence-Extensions":{"kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Trees-Arborescence-Extensions","type":"topic","title":"Extensions to Arborescence","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Members other modules add to "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Arborescence","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/trees-arborescence-extensions"},"doc://Trees/documentation/Trees/RootedTree":{"abstract":[{"text":"A tree with a root: an undirected ","type":"text"},{"code":"Graph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"code":"root","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"parent(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"children(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"depth(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the queries tree algorithms start from. The vertices, edges and their","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions are the tree’s; the root orders ","type":"text"},{"code":"children(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (each vertex’s incident edges in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position order, without the edge to its parent) and so ","type":"text"},{"code":"preorder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/trees\/rootedtree","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RootedTree","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RootedTree","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/RootedTree","kind":"symbol","title":"RootedTree"},"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/Trees/Forest/init(_:in:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/Trees\/Forest\/init(_:in:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The spanning forest as a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Forest","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" of the graph it came from.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/trees\/forest\/init(_:in:)","title":"init(_:in:)","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"SpanningForest","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Grafluent/documentation/Grafluent/Extensions":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The members each module adds to types declared in another module, by extended type."}],"role":"collectionGroup","url":"\/documentation\/grafluent\/extensions","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Grafluent\/documentation\/Grafluent\/Extensions","kind":"article","title":"Extensions Across Modules"},"doc://ShortestPaths/documentation/ShortestPaths/Trees/Forest/init(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ShortestPaths\/documentation\/ShortestPaths\/Trees\/Forest\/init(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/shortestpaths\/trees\/forest\/init(_:)","type":"topic","title":"init(_:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Distance","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"ShortestPathTree","preciseIdentifier":"s:13ShortestPaths0A8PathTreeV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"G","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Distance","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">)","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The shortest-path forest of a search from any number of sources, with the edges’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directions and the roots dropped: every reached vertex, in the tree’s index order as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists them (unreached ones left out), and one edge (parent, child) per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reached vertex with a parent, in that order. Edge positions are the forest’s own: edge k"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"joins the k-th listed vertex with a parent to its parent; the graph’s edge stays"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tree.parentEdge(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":". O(n); the vertices are hashed once, into the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"forest’s lookup table, unless they are the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":"s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<k"},{"type":"text","text":" in order."}]}}}